.Pp
If the
.Fl p
.\" undocumented redundant alias
.\" or
.\" .Fl P
flag is specified, then full file permissions and access times are
copied too.
.Pp
If the
.Fl R
.\" undocumented redundant alias
.\" or
.\" .Fl r
flag is specified then directories will be copied recursively.
Note that
.Nm
does not follow symbolic links when performing recursive transfers.
.It Xo Ic putv
.Op Fl afpR
.Ar local-path
.Op Ar remote-path
.Xc
Upload
.Ar local-path
and verify its integrity after transfer.
Equivalent to
.Ic put
with the
.Fl V
flag set.
.It Ic pwd
Display remote working directory.
.It Ic quit
Quit
.Nm hpnsftp .
.It Xo Ic reget
.Op Fl fpRV
.Ar remote-path
.Op Ar local-path
.Xc
Resume download of
.Ar remote-path .
Equivalent to
.Ic get
with the
.Fl a
flag set.
.Pp
If the
.Fl V
flag is also specified, the resume is hash-verified.
When the local file is shorter than the remote file, the XXH3 hash of the
local partial file is compared against the corresponding prefix of the
remote file using the
.Cm hpn-check-file@hpnssh.org
extension; matching hashes resume from the end of the local file, differing
hashes truncate and restart.
When the two files are the same size, the
.Cm sftp-hash-range@hpnssh.org
extension (when advertised) hashes and compares both files in 64 MiB chunks
and re-fetches only the differing chunks, catching sparse-zero holes left by
a crashed parallel-streams transfer without re-pulling the whole file; if the
server does not advertise it, the full file is hashed end-to-end instead.
The
.Ic regetv
command is a shorthand for
.Ic reget Fl V .
.It Xo Ic regetv
.Op Fl fpR
.Ar remote-path
.Op Ar local-path
.Xc
Resume download of
.Ar remote-path
with hash verification.
Equivalent to
.Ic reget
with the
.Fl V
flag set.
.It Xo Ic reput
.Op Fl fpRV
.Ar local-path
.Op Ar remote-path
.Xc
Resume upload of
.Ar local-path .
Equivalent to
.Ic put
with the
.Fl a
flag set.
.Pp
If the
.Fl V
flag is also specified, the resume is hash-verified, in the same manner as
.Ic reget Fl V
but in the upload direction: a shorter remote file resumes from its verified
prefix, and a same-size remote file is compared chunk-by-chunk via
.Cm sftp-hash-range@hpnssh.org
so only differing 64 MiB chunks are re-sent.
The
.Ic reputv
command is a shorthand for
.Ic reput Fl V .
.It Xo Ic reputv
.Op Fl fpR
.Ar local-path
.Op Ar remote-path
.Xc
Resume upload of
.Ar local-path
with hash verification.
Equivalent to
.Ic reput
with the
.Fl V
flag set.
.It Ic rename Ar oldpath newpath
Rename remote file from
.Ar oldpath
to
.Ar newpath .
.It Ic rm Ar path
Delete remote file specified by
.Ar path .
.It Ic rmdir Ar path
Remove remote directory specified by
.Ar path .
.It Ic symlink Ar oldpath newpath
Create a symbolic link from
.Ar oldpath
to
.Ar newpath .
.It Ic version
Display the
.Nm
protocol version.
.It Ic \&! Ns Ar command
Execute
.Ar command
in local shell.
.It Ic \&!
Escape to local shell.
.It Ic \&?
Synonym for help.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 on success and >0 if an error occurs.
.Pp
As an HPNSSH extension, when integrity verification is requested
.Pq Fl V , Ic getv , or Ic putv
and one or more files fail the post-transfer XXH3 integrity check, the
transfer is completed but
.Nm
exits with code 57
.Pq Dv SFTP_EX_VERIFY_FAILED
and prints a summary of the files that did not match their source. This
distinct code lets automation detect a silent-corruption event separately
from an ordinary transfer error.
